{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/271725-monsters-via-wikipedia","id":271725,"title":"monsters via wikipedia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-03T13:57:33-07:00","id":271725,"title":"monsters via wikipedia","content":"Ive bookmarked so many freakin pages about this mythological creature, or that cultures ancient religious beliefs...my. bookmark list reads like a small wiki in itself. So id like you to do the work for me! Let me know what are some of the beasties you have found and adapted with dread powers and numina from a long night of wikipedia scrolling through the weirdness that is human history. My favorite was going through giants-jotun, ettins, nephilim, troll, ogre...so many links, I eas able to come up with about 5 different types of giant with slightly different powers, different weaknesses, and style of personality/play. And dont get me started on Zoroastrianism and jinn and their cousins or rivals...that was a while nights worth!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T16:37:04-07:00","id":271856,"title":"","content":"I won't talk much about stats, but the classic monster to set against Hunters for me is always a zombie apocalypse, having the undead rise up and needing to be put down. Being a fan of zombie flicks and especially the original trilogy of the dead by Romero, I love that kind of stuff...<br /> <br /> Another fave of mine, which you could mine and find a whole load of creatures to stat up are of course the Yokai and Obakemono from Japanese folklore... Lots of cool beasts that you can add to a game, though many have already shown up in various forms as potential hobgoblins from the Hedge, but... at least in that way you don't have to wonder how to get a traditional Japanese monster over to the West for your Hunters to hunt down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:46:27-07:00","id":282294,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitsune\" target=\"_blank\">Kitsune</a>, Vampires (don't judge me) and Star Trek-brand <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RubberForeheadAliens\" target=\"_blank\">rubber-forehead aliens</a> (I'm a big Trek fan.) All run as modified Spirit-Claimed/Urged/Ridden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:22:55-07:00","id":282357,"title":"","content":"I suggest getting into the <i>Shin Megami Tensei </i>and <i>Persona </i>series from Atlus. They revolve heavily around monsters from various cultures, mythologies, folklores, and the such. Despite being called demons, the creatures range from Abrahamic monsters to Japanses-specific beasts to fairy creatures; it runs the entire gamut. Granted, it has a slight focus on the various deities of specific cultures, but there is more than enough generic monsters to keep you busy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://megamitensei.wikia.com/wiki/Megami_Tensei_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link to the wiki.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}